      "message": "My first thought was that LPTIM has 1ms resolution, so we wouldn\u0027t have benefits from applying that change.\n\nNow I\u0027m sure that resolution is 125us, so yes, it would be good to apply that change. Unfortunately it\u0027s not easy because LPTIM can overflow between reading it around `t0 \u003d get_time()` and setting alarm in `set_lptim_event()`.\n\nI\u0027m checking assembly output and it looks like the code works properly only when LPTIM doesn\u0027t overflow, so there is a field for some improvements.\n\nI think it would be good to make LPTIM fixes in separate CL.",
